e classification tasks), no material ethical-risk pathway is visible in the supplied text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-029","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The experiments utilize the MNIST and CIFAR-10 datasets, which are standard, publicly available benchmarks for image classification. The paper does not mention the use of human subjects, personally identifiable information, or sensitive data. Consequently, there are no visible privacy violations or consent issues. However, the paper does not explicitly state the licensing terms under which these datasets were used or confirm compliance with specific data usage policies, as this is not a primary focus of the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Pratik Chaudhari, Anna Choromanska, Stefano Soatto, Yann LeCun), their institutional affiliations (UCLA, NYU, Facebook AI Research), and their email addresses on the first page. The acknowledgements section also lists specific funding agencies (ONR, AFOSR, ARO). While these details are standard for a published version, the supplied evidence does not include a frozen venue or year-specific anonymity policy to determine if this constitutes a double-blind violation. Therefore, the presence of identifying information is noted, but no policy violation can be declared based solely on the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied paper text does not contain any explicit disclosures of plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. There is no evidence of textual or figure overlap with other works, nor any mention of simultaneous submission to other venues. As the corpus build lacks frozen plagiarism-overlap evidence, the absence of such disclosures in the text is insufficient to prove originality or the absence of dual submission, but no specific misconduct is indicated by the visible content.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. It also does not specify software or data licenses beyond the implicit use of standard public datasets. Since the supplied evidence does not include a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents for this venue or year, the absence of these items is noted as a limitation of the visible evidence rather than a confirmed compliance failure. The paper focuses on technical contributions without addressing societal implications.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5a5b88a08a6de14f5230ba215fd908340ee0cb102da78dc03eeea24050aa48a9","paper_id":"B1YfAfcgl","paper_ordinal":12,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"762825c2f03a7b9f19492b1c83f8ef59ca8a78f4459a60c2e87f950d49f78a86","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1YfAfcgl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"90ae58c3e517c3994b003bdd0895110944eca6463236b6968b2d84f6e8a778cc","request_identity_sha256":"592425b9665d6aca47cd41b462f0f187e7530dab016414aed14fde251434def6","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":868,"prompt_tokens":18773,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19641},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"592425b9665d6aca47cd41b462f0f187e7530dab016414aed14fde251434def6","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}